IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC, phase 2: WHERE THE CAST COMES FROM.
--
-- A party type is normally open. `Tenant HAS name IS A STRING` has one
-- constructor and infinitely many values, so "every tenant" is not something
-- the machine can count out. The spec says so itself (§2.2.7.5 point 5: the
-- pattern form "ranges over an open type and needs §2.1's `WHO member_of …`
-- filter"), and every runnable example in it draws its cast from a list.
--
-- So the cast is drawn from the ROLL. THIS FILE IS THE OLDER SPELLING of it:
-- the list an `elem <variable> <list>` condition inside `WHO` names. The rest
-- of the `WHO` condition then narrows it, and the cast word narrows it again.
-- Without such a condition there is nothing to call the roll from, and running
-- the rule refuses and says so.
--
-- Since 2026-09-08 the roll can be said outright instead — `EVERY Tenant t IN
-- tenants` — and that is the spelling to reach for; see run-in.l4, and
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC section 11.0.2.
--
-- THE OLDER SPELLING IS DEPRECATED as of 2026-09-08 (spec section 13.5), and
-- the rest of the corpus was migrated off it on 2026-09-09. THIS FILE WAS NOT,
-- deliberately: a spelling that still runs still needs tests, and this is the
-- file that tests it. If a future change removes the inference, this file is
-- what will go red, and that is the point of it.
--
-- Note in particular that its `circular` case below could NOT simply be
-- rewritten with `IN`: the explicit form catches that mistake at check time,
-- so the run-time refusal this file witnesses would have nowhere left to be
-- seen. That is why the deprecation was a migration and not a removal.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol
noOne       MEANS EMPTY

-- 1. No roll: nothing says who the tenants are, so running this refuses,
--    naming what to write instead.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`unrolled` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) WITHIN 14

#TRACE `unrolled` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1

-- 2. The cast word narrows the roll. The roll here holds a landlord as well,
--    and `Tenant` leaves him out: only Alice is bound, and only she signs.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`tenants only` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t (LIST alice, theLandlord)
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `tenants only` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1

-- 3. No cast word at all: every entry of the roll is bound, landlord included,
--    so this one needs both signatures.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`everyone listed` MEANS
    EVERY x
        WHO    elem x (LIST alice, theLandlord)
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY x)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `everyone listed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Sign theLandlord AT 2

-- 4. A further condition beside the membership one. The roll is the three
--    tenants; the second half of the condition drops Carol, so two signatures
--    are enough.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`all but carol` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t tenants AND NOT (t EQUALS carol)
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `all but carol` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2

-- 5. The roll may not mention the member it is drawing. The list is read
--    once, before there is anybody to be a member, so a roll that depended on
--    one would have to know its own answer. Refused by name; without the check
--    it reached the evaluator as an unbound name.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`circular` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t (LIST t, alice)
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14

#TRACE `circular` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1

-- 6. An empty cast. Nobody is bound, so a barrier's "all of them have acted"
--    holds from the start and the HENCE fires at once.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`nobody` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t noOne
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `nobody` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
